1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,500
Clinical trial eligibility screening is broken.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,800
While large language models can parse free text, they fail on strict medical calculations:

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:15,500
glucocorticoid potency conversions, relative washout windows, and CTCAE laboratory thresholds.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,200
When AI guesses on eligibility, patients face lethal toxicity,

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:27,630
and clinical trials suffer devastating protocol violations.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:33,800
TrialSwarm AI solves this through a multi-agent Antigravity swarm coupled with deterministic clinical verifiers.

7
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:39,500
Extractor and Phenotyper parse trial protocols and electronic health records in parallel.

8
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:46,000
Then, Safety-Auditor executes deterministic clinical rules R1 through R5,

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,840
grounded in active oncology trials from ClinicalTrials.gov and peer-reviewed literature.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,500
Let's examine patient Marcus Vance, screened against the Mirati KRYSTAL-7 protocol.

11
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:07,000
A naive language model sees four milligrams of daily Dexamethasone, compares it to the ten-milligram ceiling,

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,200
and marks him eligible.

13
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:16,800
But TrialSwarm's Rule R1 converts Dexamethasone to twenty-six point seven milligrams Prednisone equivalent,

14
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:21,680
triggering an immediate Contraindicated verdict.

15
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:27,000
On the Antigravity swarm board, every agent's contribution is transparently logged.

16
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The Extractor extracts ten criteria with verbatim line citations.

17
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,500
The Phenotyper grounds fourteen clinical facts.

18
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:41,000
And Rule R2 catches another critical trap:

19
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:48,150
a prior anti-LAG-3 checkpoint therapy ending only nineteen days ago, violating the required twenty-eight-day washout.

20
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:53,000
In the Judge console, we test our system against adversarial hallucination.

21
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,500
When an attacker or faulty model injects a fabricated quote claiming zero milligrams of steroids,

22
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:04,000
Rule R6 instantly rejects it.

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,210
If a claim is not an exact substring of the cited text lines, it is deterministically blocked.

24
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:15,000
TrialSwarm handles diverse oncology profiles seamlessly.

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,500
Patient 101 clears all criteria as Eligible.

26
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:24,200
Patient 103 is contraindicated due to thoracic radiation and grade-two liver enzymes.

27
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:30,000
And Patient 104, with a pending EGFR and ALK panel,

28
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,270
is safely routed to Needs Human Review rather than assuming a pass.

29
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:40,200
Across our benchmark of one hundred twenty synthetic oncology cases,

30
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:47,500
TrialSwarm achieved one hundred percent accuracy and zero mismatches, compared to forty-seven percent for the naive baseline.

31
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:53,000
Clinical coordinators then execute SHA-256 digital sign-offs,

32
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,630
creating a tamper-evident audit trail ready for FDA inspection.
